. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
.         *** We measure the effect of having daughters by including a variable
>  that counts the number of daughters on an individual level. 
.         ***There is a potentical endogenity problem that people with more chi
> ldren are more likly to have more daughters. There are probably unobserved fa
> ctors that determine the number of children. We will therefore include number
>  of children fixed effects.
.         *** We are adding to following control variables: gender, education, 
> log household income, being german(to account for differences in cultural att
> itudes), age, being married
.         
.         global control female age education lnhhincome married german

. 
.         reg satsocialequity num_daughter $control i.num_children, vce(cluster
